  "id": "visual-organization",
  "term": "visual organization",
  "definition": "Visual organization is the process of arranging or combining what is seen into meaningful grouped patterns that can guide action. In the source task, it meant perceiving circles as paired when line connectors linked them, which could either help or interfere with the planned movement sequence.",
